Amiga-specific library documentation
======================================

These notes document AmigaPython 2.7.18 behaviour that differs from, or
extends, the standard library.  They follow the same structure as the
Python 2.7 Library Reference (``Doc/library/*.rst``): module synopsis,
sections, ``.. function::`` / ``.. data::`` / ``.. exception::`` entries,
and Availability notes.

For portable APIs (``os``, ``os.path``, ``select``, …) read the official
docs first: https://docs.python.org/2.7/library/

Amiga-only modules and shims live under ``lib/site-python/`` (added to
``sys.path`` by ``site`` on Amiga).  The builtin ``amiga`` module is the
POSIX stand-in used by ``os``.


Module documents
---------------

=====================  =====================================================
File                   Subject
=====================  =====================================================
``amiga.rst``          Builtin ``amiga`` (POSIX + Dos + ASL/catalog/icon)
``os.rst``             ``os`` / ``os.path`` Amiga notes
``arexx.rst``          ``arexx`` / ``_arexx``
``environment.rst``    ``environment`` / ``amigavars``
``general.rst``        Platform notes (paths, Workbench, networking, …)
``other.rst``          ``select``, ``time``, ``tempfile`` Amiga notes
=====================  =====================================================


